.TH STACKGAUGE 1 "2026" "stackgauge" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
stackgauge \- static stack depth analysis for embedded firmware
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stackgauge
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIMAP_FILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B stackgauge
parses linker map files and GCC
.I .su
stack-usage files to report per-function frame sizes and, where call-graph
data is available, reported cumulative stack usage and chain depth.
.PP
Can run as a pre-commit hook to compare available stack data with thresholds.
Missing or incomplete data can pass; success does not establish a complete stack bound.
.PP
Supported toolchains: GCC + GNU ld, ARM/Keil MDK (armlink), and
ESP-IDF (Xtensa/GCC), Keil C51/LX51 and Rust/lld. The map format is auto-detected unless overridden
with
.BR \-\-toolchain .
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I MAP_FILE
Linker map file to analyse. Required unless an ELF path is supplied by CLI or config.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-elf \fIFILE\fR
Read DWARF .debug_info function ranges and scan ARM Thumb or Xtensa instruction
bytes for frame sizes. Replaces .su inputs; does not provide an ELF-only call graph.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-su\-dir " " \fIDIR\fR
Search
.I DIR
recursively for
.I .su
files. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-su\-file \fIFILE\fR
Add a single
.I .su
file explicitly. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-cgraph\-dir \fIDIR\fR
Search
.I DIR
recursively for
.I *.cgraph
dumps. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-cgraph\-file \fIFILE\fR
Add a single
.I .cgraph
file explicitly. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude\-dir \fINAME\fR
Skip directories named
.I NAME
during
.I .su
/
.I .cgraph
search. Repeatable. CompilerIdC, CompilerIdCXX, and CompilerIdASM are
excluded by default.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-stack\-threshold " " \fIN\fR
Fail (exit 1) if the reported chain, or the largest frame when no chain is
available, exceeds
.I N
bytes.
.TP
.B \-\-depth\-threshold \fIN\fR
Fail (exit 1) if reported call-chain depth exceeds
.I N
(ARM/Keil, Keil C51, or GNU ld/ESP-IDF with cgraph).
.TP
.B \-\-top\-n \fIN\fR
Number of functions to show in the report (default: 10). See also
.BR \-v .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show all functions, not just the top N.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIfmt\fR
Output format:
.B text
(default) or
.BR json .
.TP
.B \-\-toolchain \fIname\fR
Force map format:
.BR gnu\-ld " | " arm\-keil " | " esp\-idf " | " keil\-c51 " | " rust\-lld .
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Config file (default:
.IR stackgauge.toml ).
CLI scalar values override config values; search and exclusion lists combine.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No threshold exceeded by available data (or no thresholds set). Missing or
incomplete data can currently return success; this is not proof of a complete bound.
.TP
.B 1
A stack or depth threshold was exceeded.
.TP
.B 2
Fatal error (missing file, parse failure, etc.).
.SH CONFIGURATION FILE
Place a
.I stackgauge.toml
in your current working directory or pass
.B \-c
to specify a path. CLI scalar values take precedence; search and exclusion
lists combine. Relative paths are resolved from the current working directory.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.nf
stack_threshold = 2048
depth_threshold = 12
top_n = 20
su_dirs = ["build"]
# toolchain = "gnu-ld"
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Report top-10 largest frames (GNU ld):
.B stackgauge build/firmware.map --su-dir build/
.TP
With static call-chain analysis:
.B stackgauge build/firmware.map --su-dir build/ --cgraph-dir build/
.TP
Fail if reported chain/largest frame > 2 KB or reported depth > 12:
.B stackgauge build/firmware.map --su-dir build/ --stack-threshold 2048 --depth-threshold 12
.TP
JSON output:
.B stackgauge firmware.map --su-dir build/ --format json | jq .call_graph
.TP
ARM/Keil text input (recognized call-graph sections must be in the same file):
.B stackgauge build/firmware.map
.SH PRE-COMMIT INTEGRATION
Add to
.I .pre-commit-config.yaml:
.PP
.nf
repos:
  - repo: local
    hooks:
      - id: stackgauge
        name: Stack depth analysis
        language: system
        entry: stackgauge
        args: [build/firmware.map, --su-dir=build/]
        pass_filenames: false
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gcc (1),
.BR ld (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Brandon Arrendondo
.SH LIMITATIONS
Armlink separate .htm/.txt reports are not automatically discovered or parsed as HTML.
Indirect calls, missing frames and unknown components can leave lower bounds.
ELF scans recognize selected instructions and omit zero or unrecognized frames.
